e an idea more brain dead than a moratorium on data centers.", "display_text_range": [0, 80], "facets": []}, "author": {"screen_name": "unclebobmartin", "url": "https://x.com/unclebobmartin", "id": "9505092", "followers": 282563, "following": 366, "likes": 7447, "media_count": 2721, "statuses": 46580, "name": "Uncle Bob Martin", "description": "Software Craftsman", "raw_description": {"text": "Software Craftsman", "facets": []}, "location": "iPhone: 56.802658,9.868149", "banner_url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_banners/9505092/1774556131", "avatar_url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2037262183751704577/54AiU968_200x200.jpg", "joined": "Wed Oct 17 19:03:34 +0000 2007", "protected": false, "website": {"url": "http://cleancoder.com", "display_url": "cleancoder.com"}, "verification": {"verified": true, "verified_at": null, "type": "individual"}, "type": "profile"}, "replies": 51, "reposts": 31, "likes": 761, "bookmarks": 17, "quotes": 3, "embed_card": "tweet", "created_at": "Tue Aug 25 10:34:07 +0000 2026", "created_timestamp": 1787654047, "views": 28698, "is_note_tweet": false, "community_note": null, "lang": "en", "replying_to": null, "media": {}, "provider": "twitter", "reposted_by": null}, {"type": "status", "url": "https://x.com/unclebobmartin/status/2091890518942679110", "id": "2091890518942679110", "text": "My current loop (It changes every week or so)\n\n1. Run the app.  Discover issues.  Have an agent diagnose and add issues to issues.md.\n2. Have agent fix issues.md.\n3. Have agent audit the fixes.\n4. Have agent repair what it did wrong.\n5. Go to 1.\n\nOr something roughly like that.", "raw_text": {"text": "My current loop (It changes every week or so)\n\n1. Run the app.  Discover issues.  Have an agent diagnose and add issues to issues.md.\n2. Have agent fix issues.md.\n3. Have agent audit the fixes.\n4. Have agent repair what it did wrong.\n5. Go to 1.\n\nOr something roughly like that.", "display_text_range": [0, 278], "facets": []}, "author": {"screen_name": "unclebobmartin", "url": "https://x.com/unclebobmartin", "id": "9505092", "followers": 282563, "following": 366, "likes": 7447, "media_count": 2721, "statuses": 46580, "name": "Uncle Bob Martin", "description": "Software Craftsman", "raw_description": {"text": "Software Craftsman", "facets": []}, "location": "iPhone: 56.802658,9.868149", "banner_url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_banners/9505092/1774556131", "avatar_url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2037262183751704577/54AiU968_200x200.jpg", "joined": "Wed Oct 17 19:03:34 +0000 2007", "protected": false, "website": {"url": "http://cleancoder.com", "display_url": "cleancoder.com"}, "verification": {"verified": true, "verified_at": null, "type": "individual"}, "type": "profile"}, "replies": 97, "reposts": 61, "likes": 1237, "bookmarks": 701, "quotes": 7, "embed_card": "tweet", "created_at": "Mon Aug 24 14:08:59 +0000 2026", "created_timestamp": 1787580539, "views": 71165, "is_note_tweet": false, "community_note": null, "lang": "en", "replying_to": null, "media": {}, "provider": "twitter", "reposted_by": null}, {"type": "status", "url": "https://x.com/unclebobmartin/status/2091883431529447444", "id": "2091883431529447444", "text": "Agents read all kinds of left over rule files.  For example, grok reads ~/.claude/Claude.md.  \n\nIf you are not aware of this, it can lead to strange contradictions and confusions.", "raw_text": {"text": "Agents read all kinds of left over rule files.  For example, grok reads ~/.claude/Claude.md.  \n\nIf you are not aware of this, it can lead to strange contradictions and confusions.", "display_text_range": [0, 179], "facets": []}, "author": {"screen_name": "unclebobmartin", "url": "https://x.com/unclebobmartin", "id": "9505092", "followers": 282563, "following": 366, "likes": 7447, "media_count": 2721, "statuses": 46580, "name": "Uncle Bob Martin", "description": "Software Craftsman", "raw_description": {"text": "Software Craftsman", "facets": []}, "location": "iPhone: 56.802658,9.868149", "banner_url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_banners/9505092/1774556131", "avatar_url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2037262183751704577/54AiU968_200x200.jpg", "joined": "Wed Oct 17 19:03:34 +0000 2007", "protected": false, "website": {"url": "http://cleancoder.com", "display_url": "cleancoder.com"}, "verification": {"verified": true, "verified_at": null, "type": "individual"}, "type": "profile"}, "replies": 34, "reposts": 6, "likes": 286, "bookmarks": 39, "quotes": 2, "embed_card": "tweet", "created_at": "Mon Aug 24 13:40:50 +0000 2026", "created_timestamp": 1787578850, "views": 19173, "is_note_tweet": false, "community_note": null, "lang": "en", "replying_to": null, "media": {}, "provider": "twitter", "reposted_by": null}, {"type": "status", "url": "https://x.com/unclebobmartin/status/2091876658898706474", "id": "2091876658898706474", "text": "Agents are not particularly good and conceptual encapsulation.  That's because they don't understand what concepts are important to a human software engineer.  \n\nFor example, I have a chain of operations.  Some chains are two long, some four, some six.  The last in the chain messages all the others regarding completion.  \n\nI had the agents build the six long chain first.  They made the decision that \"done\" was indicated by a message with multiple recipients, rather than by the sender being at the end of the chain. \n\nThe human concept of \"the end of the chain\" did not have the sense of doneness to the agents that it would to a human software engineer.  \n\nI discovered this misconception during an audit.", "raw_text": {"text": "Agents are not particularly good and conceptual encapsulation.  That's because they don't understand what concepts are important to a human software engineer.  \n\nFor example, I have a chain of operations.  Some chains are two long, some four, some six.  The last in the chain messages all the others regarding completion.  \n\nI had the agents build the six long chain first.  They made the decision that \"done\" was indicated by a message with multiple recipients, rather than by the sender being at the end of the chain. \n\nThe human concept of \"the end of the chain\" did not have the sense of doneness to the agents that it would to a human software engineer.  \n\nI discovered this misconception during an audit.", "display_text_range": [0, 710], "facets": []}, "author": {"screen_name": "unclebobmartin", "url": "https://x.com/unclebobmartin", "id": "9505092", "followers": 282563, "following": 366, "likes": 7447, "media_count": 2721, "statuses": 46580, "name": "Uncle Bob Martin", "description": "Software Craftsman", "raw_description": {"text": "Software Craftsman", "facets": []}, "location": "iPhone: 56.802658,9.868149", "banner_url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_banners/9505092/1774556131", "avatar_url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2037262183751704577/54AiU968_200x200.jpg", "joined": "Wed Oct 17 19:03:34 +0000 2007", "protected": false, "website": {"url": "http://cleancoder.com", "display_url": "cleancoder.com"}, "verification": {"verified": true, "verified_at": null, "type": "individual"}, "type": "profile"}, "replies": 43, "reposts": 20, "likes": 424, "bookmarks": 156, "quotes": 2, "embed_card": "tweet", "created_at": "Mon Aug 24 13:13:55 +0000 2026", "created_timestamp": 1787577235, "views": 47027, "is_note_tweet": true, "community_note": null, "lang": "en", "replying_to": null, "media": {}, "provider": "twitter", "reposted_by": null}, {"type": "status", "url": "https://x.com/unclebobmartin/status/2091874328610505120", "id": "2091874328610505120", "text": "I still use clojure.  The experiments I've run suggest that python and clojure are the most efficient languages for the agents to use.  These experiments were done some months back, and were not controlled.  So you should consider this as little more than an anecdote.", "raw_text": {"text": "I still use clojure.  The experiments I've run suggest that python and clojure are the most efficient languages for the agents to use.  These experiments were done some months back, and were not controlled.  So you should consider this as little more than an anecdote.", "display_text_range": [0, 268], "facets": []}, "author": {"screen_name": "unclebobmartin", "url": "https://x.com/unclebobmartin", "id": "9505092", "followers": 282563, "following": 366, "likes": 7447, "media_count": 2721, "statuses": 46580, "name": "Uncle Bob Martin", "description": "Software Craftsman", "raw_description": {"text": "Software Craftsman", "facets": []}, "location": "iPhone: 56.802658,9.868149", "banner_url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_banners/9505092/1774556131", "avatar_url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2037262183751704577/54AiU968_200x200.jpg", "joined": "Wed Oct 17 19:03:34 +0000 2007", "protected": false, "website": {"url": "http://cleancoder.com", "display_url": "cleancoder.com"}, "verification": {"verified": true, "verified_at": null, "type": "individual"}, "type": "profile"}, "replies": 37, "reposts": 10, "likes": 177, "bookmarks": 33, "quotes": 4, "embed_card": "tweet", "created_at": "Mon Aug 24 13:04:39 +0000 2026", "created_timestamp": 1787576679, "views": 21309, "is_note_tweet": false, "community_note": null, "lang": "en", "replying_to": null, "media": {}, "provider": "twitter", "reposted_by": null}, {"type": "status", "url": "https://x.com/unclebobmartin/status/2091869198980887007", "id": "2091869198980887007", "text": "When you ask the agent to audit its recent activity (which you should always do), make sure you read it's responses very carefully.  Especially the part where it talks about gaps and things that were NOT done.  You'll often be surprised.", "raw_text": {"text": "When you ask the agent to audit its recent activity (which you should always do), make sure you read it's responses very carefully.  Especially the part where it talks about gaps and things that were NOT done.  You'll often be surprised.", "dis